Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 16:50:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] consent history: patients get a permanent, versioned
 record of every grant and withdrawal
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

  - contract V3.1 addendum (SS11): seventh owner-scoped operation
    GET /api/comfort-profile/consent/history -> 200|401, newest-first, no 403 path
  - every grant/withdraw row now records consentVersion, consentTextHash (sha256 of the
    exact statement shown) and purpose — additive fields, append-only, never rewritten;
    rows recorded before versioning surface a legacy note instead
  - the consent statement lives server-side (single source of truth) and is rendered
    verbatim in the grant UI; wording changes require a version bump
  - ConsentHistoryTimeline (pure presentation) renders the timeline below the shell;
    currently-shared categories show as read-only chips while consent is active
  - tests/consent-history.api.test.mjs: 7 checks — 401, hash consistency, scoped+versioned
    grant, newest-first timeline, owner isolation, notes-never-leak, failed-grant purity
